+
+                    // Certification mode: mirror the PrplOS (WHM/ambiorix) behaviour and bring
+                    // the BSS down WITHOUT removing the interface, the hostapd BSS config or
+                    // the persistent UCI section.
+                    //
+                    // Why this is needed for certification: dev_reset_default tears down every
+                    // BSS before each test case. On nl80211/hostapd, removing a BSS interface
+                    // (remove_bss / remove_interface / LINK_REMOVE) destroys the netdev. When
+                    // the removed BSS is the radio's primary interface this brings the whole
+                    // radio down - the fronthaul ap_manager loses its hostapd control socket,
+                    // terminates, and son_slave runs agent_reset(), so the radio and its daemon
+                    // go down and the VAPs are left disabled. The destructive path also rewrote
+                    // the persistent prplmesh.hostap_iface (promoting the next BSS to
+                    // "interface="), so every reset left the agent pointing at a different radio
+                    // interface and state drifted across test cases.
+                    //
+                    // WHM's ap_wlan_hal_whm::update_vap_credentials() only sets
+                    // AccessPoint.Enable=false for a torn-down BSS. STOP_AP is the hostapd
+                    // equivalent: the BSS stops beaconing and deauthenticates its clients while
+                    // the netdev, the hostapd BSS config and the radio all stay alive, so the
+                    // following dev_set_config can re-enable the BSS with new credentials
+                    // (enable_all_fh_vaps() brings it back with RELOAD).
+                    //
+                    // Outside certification mode the original destructive behaviour is kept
+                    // unchanged, so normal deployments are not affected by this change.
+                    if (get_hal_conf().certification_mode) {
+                        LOG(INFO) << "[CERT] BSS " << vap_info.bss << " (vap_id " << vap_id
